            "text": "An efficient and robust Python program to solve this problem:\n\n```python\nimport json\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\ndef main():\n    totals = defaultdict(int)\n    chunksize = 250_000\n    \n    # Process transactions.csv in chunks to balance memory use and performance\n    for chunk in pd.read_csv(\n        'transactions.csv',\n        usecols=['account_id', 'category', 'amount_cents'],\n        chunksize=chunksize,\n    ):\n        acc = chunk['account_id']\n        mask = (acc % 11) < 7\n        if not mask.any():\n            continue\n        \n        filtered = chunk[mask]\n        acc_filt = filtered['account_id']\n        mult = (acc_filt % 97) + 1\n        amt = filtered['amount_cents']\n        \n        # Check whether int64 arithmetic is guaranteed not to overflow for this chunk\n        safe_for_int64 = False\n        if pd.api.types.is_integer_dtype(amt) and pd.api.types.is_integer_dtype(acc_filt):\n            min_val, max_val = int(amt.min()), int(amt.max())\n            max_abs = max(abs(min_val), abs(max_val))\n            # 9e18 is below int64 max (approx 9.22e18)\n            if max_abs * 97 * len(filtered) < 9_000_000_000_000_000_000:\n                safe_for_int64 = True\n        \n        if safe_for_int64:\n            prod = amt * mult\n            chunk_sums = prod.groupby(filtered['category'], sort=False).sum()\n        else:\n            # Fallback to arbitrary precision Python integers\n            prod = amt.astype(object) * mult.astype(object)\n            chunk_sums = prod.groupby(filtered['category'], sort=False).sum()\n            \n        for cat, val in chunk_sums.items():\n            totals[str(cat)] += int(val)\n            \n    print(f\"TOTAL:{json.dumps(totals, sort_keys=True)}\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n```",
